FAQ = [
 ("What is the best bed rack for a Jeep Gladiator?",
  "For a rooftop tent, the RealTruck GoRack (9150101). It is a mid-height aluminum and steel rack rated for 1,000 lb static and 600 lb dynamic, with T-slots on all four sides of the side rails, MOLLE side panels and a limited lifetime warranty, and RealTruck lists it at $1,089.99. It can also mount to a bed cover with T-slot rails, which few racks can. If you don't run a cover and want to spend about half as much, the Rough Country 10620 (750 lb static, 400 lb dynamic, from $499.95) is the value pick."),
 ("Why do Gladiator owners use bed racks instead of roof racks?",
  "Because the Gladiator's roof comes off. Every JT has a removable hardtop or soft top, so there is no fixed roof to carry a rooftop tent or heavy crossbars the way a four-door pickup would. The bed is the only solid structure behind the cab, which makes a bed rack the usual platform for a tent, an awning, recovery boards and fuel cans."),
 ("Does a bed rack fit a Gladiator with the Trail Rail system?",
  "It depends on how the rack mounts. The Mopar Trail Rail kit is a 52 in front rail and two 48 in side rails, and Quadratec lists its vertical capacity at 250 lb per rail side, which is less than any tent rack's rating. Racks that clamp to the bed rail lip can conflict with the side rails; racks that drill into the bed, like the Rough Country 10620, work around them. Yakima says tracked beds need its Track Kit 1 or 2. Confirm Trail Rail compatibility with the seller before you order."),
 ("Can I run a tonneau cover and a bed rack on a Gladiator?",
  "Yes, but only with a matched pair. RealTruck says the GoRack mounts to any bed cover with a T-slot style rail system. Yakima sells a Tonneau Kit 1 for select covers. On JeepGladiatorForum, owners report running Pace Edwards roll-up covers under Yakima-style T-slot racks and pairing a Diamondback HD cover with a rack that bolts to the cover's anchor points. Budget clamp racks such as the OTHOWE 22 in are listed as not compatible with a tonneau cover."),
 ("What is the difference between static and dynamic load ratings?",
  "Dynamic is what the rack can carry while the truck is moving, including bumps, braking and body roll. Static is what it can hold parked, which is the number that matters when people are sleeping in a rooftop tent. The GoRack is rated 1,000 lb static and 600 lb dynamic; the Rough Country 10620 750 lb static and 400 lb dynamic. Yakima rates the OverHaul HD at 500 lb on-road and 300 lb off-road. The tent and everything strapped to the rack must stay under the dynamic figure on the road."),
 ("Do I have to drill my Gladiator bed to install a rack?",
  "Not for every rack. Rough Country says its 10620 requires drilling and bolting directly to the bed, and recommends its 10583 nutsert tool. Clamp racks such as the Yakima OverHaul HD (BedGrip clamps) and the budget SUORTO and OTHOWE racks grip the bed rails instead. The GoRack can use the stake pockets. If you want an untouched bed, read the install sheet before you buy."),
 ("Which rack height works best with a Gladiator rooftop tent?",
  "Mid-height racks near the cab roofline are the common choice because the tent rides partly in the cab's wind shadow and the truck stays easier to park. The Gladiator's roof panels come off, so many owners also want a tent that clears a removed top. Full-height racks such as the OTHOWE 22 in give the most room under the tent for a fridge or bins. Yakima's OverHaul HD adjusts from 19 to 30 in if you can't decide."),
 ("How much weight can a Gladiator carry on a bed rack?",
  "Less than the rack ratings suggest. Wikipedia gives the Gladiator's payload as 1,000 lb at the minimum and 1,700 lb at the maximum, depending on configuration. That payload covers passengers, the rack itself, the tent and everything in the bed. Yakima lists the OverHaul HD towers alone at 59.52 lb before crossbars. Check the payload on your door-jamb sticker, subtract people and gear, and plan the rack load from what is left."),
 ("Will a Gladiator bed rack block the tailgate or third brake light?",
  "Most racks sit on the bed sides and leave the tailgate free, but the crossbars and anything on them can sit behind the cab-mounted third brake light. Mid-height racks and loads kept low reduce the problem. Rough Country notes its rack preserves rear visibility. After install, turn on the brake lights and check from behind the truck that the center light is still visible with your usual load."),
 ("Does the Rough Country 10620 fit the Mojave and Rubicon?",
  "Yes. Rough Country's product page lists the 10620 for the 2020–2026 Gladiator JT 4WD, including the standard truck, Rubicon and Mojave. Every Gladiator has the same 5 ft bed, so there's no bed-length choice to get wrong. Rough Country also notes that this rack does not work with its own hard-shell rooftop tent, so pair it with a different tent."),
]

